{
    "background_story": "Colton was a brilliant and eccentric professor of ancient mythology. His fascination with the Greek goddess of memory, Mnemosyne, led him to dedicate his life's work to unlocking the secrets of human memory. He spent years studying the ancient arts of mnemonics, developing innovative techniques to enhance recall and retention. Colton's obsession with Mnemosyne's realm extended beyond academia; he believed that memories held the key to understanding the human experience. He created an elaborate memory palace, a labyrinthine repository of knowledge and recollections, which he claimed allowed him to tap into the collective unconscious. Colton's students revered him for his uncanny ability to recall even the most obscure mythological details, and his groundbreaking research earned him international recognition. Though some whispered that his fixation on Mnemosyne bordered on madness, Colton knew that his work would forever change the way humanity understood the power of memory.",
